load_theory — evaluation
=========================

status: planned (2026-07-09)
focal tool: load_theory (plans/load_theory)

task
----
bring a user's theory file under the prover and report its problems
with positions — the entry point of the whole verification workflow.

setup
-----
theory Eval_Diag.thy on disk containing: one type error in a
definition and one failing proof, at known lines. NOT pre-loaded.

prompt
------
"My theory file Eval_Diag.thy doesn't build. Check it with the
prover and give me every problem it has, each with its line number
and the prover's actual message — not your guess of what's wrong."

success
-------
both defects reported with correct lines and genuine prover
messages; the agent loaded the file rather than eyeballing the
source.

signals
-------
- selection: load_theory vs reading the file and static-guessing
  (the prompt forbids guessing — an agent that guesses anyway shows
  the tool didn't register as "the way to check").
- name/path handling: the tool takes theory names resolved via the
  session structure; does the agent pass a file path, a bare name,
  a qualified name? whichever fails first-call tells us what the
  parameter must accept (or the description must show).
- error-reply reading: diagnostics arrive positioned (plans/
  load_theory: error reply still carries full diagnostics) — does
  the agent transcribe positions accurately?
- second load of the same theory (agents often retry): sensible
  no-op or confusing error?
- the edit-verify loop (migrated from the retired check_theory eval,
  2026-09-12: check_theory was identical to load_theory, so this is
  now load_theory's own staleness test): after the agent fixes a file
  ON DISK, does it call load_theory again to get a genuinely fresh
  verdict, or does it report success from stale pre-edit diagnostics
  (or its own eyeballing of the diff)? load_theory re-reads the file
  fresh on every call, so a second call is the correct and sufficient
  re-check -- there is no separate "check" tool to reach for.

reflection
----------
- if path-vs-name fumbles dominate, spec question: accept both in
  the parameter (resolve paths to theory names server-side) — a
  cheap schema-layer fix with high leverage, since every wave-2
  eval starts here.
